{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-local-substrate-q","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:local-substrate-q","kind":"proposition","title":"Local Value of the Substrate Parameter","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-terminal-resolution","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-photonic-hall"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-local-substrate-q"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-from-generators","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-formula-table","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-comparison-table","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-w-boson-mass-discrepancy"],"tags":["substrate","mass","observation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Experimental.LocalSubstrateQ","text":"local-substrate-q.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/local-substrate-q.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:local-substrate-q\"></a><p>In any sufficiently small neighbourhood <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\subset M</code> of the observable universe, the substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> (<a href=\"#def:substrate-parameter\">substrate parameter</a>) satisfies</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  q\\big|_U =  1.1097 \\pm 0.001.</code></pre>\n<p>Specifically, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q|_U</code> is the unique real root <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code> of the equation:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  (1 - q^{-1})^{2} = \\frac{\\mathrm{Vol}(4_1)}{m_\\mu / m_e}.</code></pre>\n<p>Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Vol}(4_1) = 2\\,\\mathrm{Cl}_2(\\pi/3) \\approx 2.02988</code> is the hyperbolic volume of the figure-eight knot. The constant <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_\\mu / m_e \\approx 206.768</code> is the CODATA 2022 muon--electron mass ratio.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/local-substrate-q.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"16.17.3"}
